# THIS FILE DOES NOTHING. Edit deploy.sh instead.
#
# .rscignore is an R rsconnect feature. rsconnect-python does not read it — the
# string appears nowhere in the package (checked against 1.31.1), and a test
# bundle built with a .rscignore naming two paths included both of them, plus
# the .rscignore file itself.
#
# Every exclusion has to be passed as -x/--exclude on the command line, which is
# what deploy.sh does. Deploying without it bundles ~10 GB (data/ alone is
# 9.7 GB); with it the bundle is 181 files and 3.8 MB.
#
# Kept as a signpost rather than deleted, because its former contents read as if
# they were in force and the next person to look will reach for this file first.
